Let's define $v_i = (x_{i+1} - x_i) / dt$.                                      
Then $\ddot{x}_i = (v_{i+1} - v_i) / dt = (x_{i+2} - 2x_{i+1} + x_i) / dt^2$.   
The equation is $\ddot{x} = a \dot{x} + b x + c$.                               
This can be written as $(x_{i+2} - 2x_{i+1} + x_i) / dt^2 = a (x_{i+1} - x_i) / 
dt + b x_i + c$.                                                                
Multiply by $dt^2$: $x_{i+2} - 2x_{i+1} + x_i = a \cdot dt (x_{i+1} - x_i) + b  
\cdot dt^2 x_i + c \cdot dt^2$.                                                 
Let $A = a \cdot dt$, $B = b \cdot dt^2$, $C = c \cdot dt^2$.                   
Then $x_{i+2} = (2 + A) x_{i+1} + (B - A - 1) x_i + C$.                         
This is a linear recurrence $x_{i+2} = \alpha x_{i+1} + \beta x_i + \gamma$.    
