its derivatives. Then, I'll segment the data into Mode A ($x_1' < 0$) and Mode B
($x_1' > 0$). For each mode, I'll fit the coefficients $a, b, c, d$ for the     
2nd-order ODE $x_1'' = a x_1' + b x_1 + c x_1^2 + d$. Finally, I will identify  
